# Workshop gallery, shots 4 to 6 of the SHOTLIST v3 of 2026-11-07 (THE STORY, the outfit rule, the series and the rules applied are
# in the header of 09-galerie-sanctuaire.feature; shots 1 to 3 there, 7 and 8 in 09c-galerie-chats.feature, 9 to 11 in
# 09d-galerie-chiens.feature). Second ticket of the day: afternoon and evening. Cells from SANCTUAIRE-CASES.md of NSB, coats from
# Mod/Patches (palette names), steps from PickleTools.
#
# SHOTLIST (index, name, place, hour, framing, gesture, decor, living things, outfit, what the image says, subtitle)
#
#   4. workshop-4-chess. cloister, 15h, clear, zoom 4 on (172, 126) (8 cells tall, about 19 px a cell at 268 px wide, a Yorkshire
#           about 14 px), +20 then +30 then +15 ticks. TIGHT shot of the series. Light under the roof plus the torches. Gesture:
#           Nelim, no hat (roofed), denim Apparel_CollarShirt dyed rgb (44, 86, 140), Roo_HD_Hair_Highpony, hair colour
#           rgb (56, 36, 18), a smirk and a squint (MouthSmirkSmile, LidSquinting: she is about to win; fallback smile), first
#           stands at (172, 127) facing South, then is forced into the job Play_Chess on the ChessTable at (172, 126), so she
#           sits facing the camera. Instant: her hand is over the board as the third dog trots in (30 ticks of play, then
#           Brume walks, 15 more ticks). Three Yorkshire terriers (Core, coats picked to differ): Tweed -1 original black and tan
#           lies (174, 127); Brume 0 slate walks (forced) from (178, 128) to (175, 127), mid-step; Brioche 1 taupe stands (176, 127)
#           facing South: the animal that faces the camera; coat 2 oatmeal is not drawn (about the original at that size).
#           Decor, a games corner: the existing ChessTable, KneelPillow, TorchLamps and columns of the colonnade, plus Plant_Daylily
#           fully grown at (170, 128) and (177, 127), a Stool at (171, 126) and at (173, 127) beside the table, TorchLamp at
#           (169, 127) lit: the board, two seats, lamps and flowers fill a tight frame. Says: Nelim is playing chess in the cloister,
#           about to win, and three Yorkshire terriers, three coats, keep her company. Estimate 5.
#           Subtitle: "A game of chess, watched from below."
#
#   5. workshop-5-evening-training. enclosure-south, 18h, clear, low sun, zoom 4.5 on (158, 210), +45 ticks. Gesture: Nelim, straw
#           Apparel_CowboyHat dyed rgb (214, 174, 92) on long loose Roo_Royal_LongHD, denim Apparel_CollarShirt dyed
#           rgb (44, 86, 140), hair colour rgb (56, 36, 18), smile, carries 2 Kibble (the treats) and is forced into the job Train on the husky Ardoise: she stands
#           beside it, turned to it. Instant: she has just given the command, the husky answers (fallback if Train does not start: a
#           forced haul of Hay to (158, 211)). Four huskies (Core, coats 0 iceblue, -1 original, 1 coffee, 2 oatmeal): Givre 0
#           spawned (157, 211) and Moka 1 spawned (161, 210) follow her within 3 cells; Ardoise -1 stands (158, 211) facing South:
#           the trained one, the animal that faces the camera; Lait 2 spawned (155, 213) lies down tired. Decor, the evening
#           pen: the fence and the laying boxes of the pen, Plant_YellowTallGrass fully grown at (156, 209), (162, 212), (154, 210),
#           (160, 208) and (163, 213), Plant_Daylily fully grown at (157, 209) and (162, 211), PlantPot_Bonsai at (163, 210),
#           TorchLamp at (156, 208) lit and at (162, 208) lit: grass all round, painted zones hidden, low sun plus two lamps.
#           Says: at dusk Nelim gathers her four huskies at the pen, the braziers lit, four coats.
#           Estimate 5. Subtitle: "Evening training, and four huskies at the gate."
#
#   6. workshop-6-fireside. fire-pit, 20h, clear, zoom 5 on (181, 115), +60 ticks. CLOSING image. Gesture: Nelim, now in the navy
#           Apparel_Duster dyed rgb (58, 58, 98) over the denim Apparel_CollarShirt dyed rgb (44, 86, 140) "because the evening is
#           cold", no hat, Roo_HD_Hair_Highpony, hair colour rgb (56, 36, 18), smile, plays the instrument Harp by the fire (the
#           harp of the ritual hall, near (207, 117), is hidden first so the step finds ours). Instant: the first notes, the corgis
#           gather. Corgis of Vanilla Animals Expanded (AEXP_Corgi, coats -1 original, 0 taupe, 1 champagne, 2 slate): Noisette -1
#           stands (182, 113) facing South: the animal that faces the camera; Praline 0 walks (forced) from (177, 116) to (179, 115)
#           towards the fire; Dune 1 stands (183, 114) facing West; Brume 2 lies asleep (179, 113); the white cat of shot 1, Neige
#           (akaNEKO_shironeko, coat -1), sleeps at (179, 117): the evening gathers the day. Decor, the fireside lived in: Harp at
#           (183, 116), PlantPot_Bonsai at (185, 117), TorchLamp at (177, 114), (184, 114) and (181, 118) lit, Brazier at (186, 114)
#           lit, Plant_Daylily fully grown at (184, 119) and (186, 119), a Stool at (178, 118), the fire itself. Says: Nelim plays
#           the harp by the fire in the cold evening, the corgis gather and the white cat of the breakfast sleeps: the day is done.
#           Estimate 5. Subtitle: "By the fire, the corgis keep their own colours."
#
# Day order (reindex at 9.b): 7h (1), 10h (2), 11h (9), 12h (3), 13h (7), 15h (4), 16h (10), 17h (8), 18h (5), 19h (11), 20h (6).
# Interface windows: none planned. Ideas kept for later, not written: the barn east extension for a twelve-cat nap room, a bridge
# parade on the river-bridge, a rain day, kittens at life stage 0, one dyed collar per dog; steps to ask NPT for (arc placement,
# sitting pose, advance until distance, a camera step on several named animals).
# RISK: shot 4 Play_Chess seat (NPT fix 7bcbcf6 needs a seat next to the table: the two Stools), shot 5 Train may not start
# (fallback above), shot 6 the harp cell.
